<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46540" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summāno</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subm-</span></b> ), āre, v.
		a. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>n</i>
			[sub-mano]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to glide</i> or <i>trickle under</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 1,
				2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to wet somewhat</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestimenta mea, ubi obdormivi ebrius, Summano
					(with a play on the name Summanus, i. e. Pluto),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Curc. 3, 46</span></i>
			 (v. the passage in connection).</div>
